WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.616
Why do states act the

2
00:00:01.616 --> 00:00:02.709
way they do?

3
00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:03.945
Each IR theory gives a

4
00:00:03.945 --> 00:00:05.388
different answer.

5
00:00:05.717 --> 00:00:08.970
Morgenthau's classical realism,

6
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.469
1948. Waltz's neo-realism,

7
00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:15.280
1979. And Wendt's 1992 essay:

8
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.296
anarchy is what states make

9
00:00:17.296 --> 00:00:18.340
of it.

10
00:00:18.659 --> 00:00:20.828
Realism: states pursue power.

11
00:00:20.828 --> 00:00:23.678
Liberalism: institutions and trade make

12
00:00:23.678 --> 00:00:25.443
cooperation possible.

13
00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:28.091
Constructivism: ideas and identities shape

14
00:00:28.091 --> 00:00:29.709
what states want.

15
00:00:30.034 --> 00:00:32.842
Marxist and feminist approaches ask

16
00:00:32.842 --> 00:00:33.625
who benefits,

17
00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:35.275
and who is left out.

18
00:00:35.942 --> 00:00:37.119
Your turn.

19
00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:38.480
Whose line?
